{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdyZKA8YVMVF45PqwMpeg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KhpwV9Y7vL5f6JLFzFaFGX","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T211427.316028Z-623ff2d9fa/repo/runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py","old_string":"    unit_graph.register_unit_path(builder, sorted(bindings))\n\n    return inventory\n\n\ndef register_workbook_topology(builder: StateGraph) -> dict[str, tuple[str, ...]]:","new_string":"    unit_graph.register_unit_path(builder, sorted(bindings))\n    register_unit_repair_path(builder, sorted(bindings))\n\n    return inventory\n\n\ndef register_unit_repair_path(builder: StateGraph, available: Sequence[str]) -> dict[str, tuple[str, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"Wire D16-D23's internal edges (spec section 8.2's repair/acceptance cycle).\n\n    Additive over the builder `register_skeleton` already added every node in\n    `available` to -- the same division of labor `unit_graph.register_unit_\n    path` uses for the normal unit path: this adds no node, only the\n    conditional edges among D16-D23 and back out to `D05`/`D98` spec section\n    8.2's own diagram describes (\"D16 PASS -> D22 -> D23 -> D05\", \"D16 FAIL ->\n    D17 -> D18 -> D19 -> D20 -> D21 -> earliest invalidated producer -> D16\",\n    \"D17/D18 repeat/attempt-bound exhaustion -> D98\").\n\n    A no-op when none of `UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` is in `available` (N30's own\n    tests call `register_skeleton` with the narrower `binding_inventory()`,\n    which must keep behaving exactly as it did before this generation); once\n    `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` passes the widened\n    `repair_acceptance_bindings()` set, every branch here is real.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    known = set(available)\n    resolved: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {}\n    for source, path in UNIT_REPAIR_BRA